description:
Aidan is a professional musician and singer and the son of two Drimoleague natives, Martin and Bridget Keane, who instilled in him a powerful passion and love for performing. Having spent the last two years touring the world with the smash hit Dubliners show “Seven Drunken Nights”, he’s delighted to share the songs and stories that inspired him in the place where it all started.

Aidan explains;
“I want to make the show very personal, sharing the important songs and the stories behind them that paved the journey that lead me from meekly singing “Stairway to Heaven” in May Deane’s when I was 14 to singing to a sold out Olympia Theatre. With the show I really want to honour how powerfully helpful a community that encourages singing and playing is. The songs will be known ones for the most part, singing will be encouraged. I’ve been using this format in Canada telling tales about Irish history and playing the songs that represent it and it’s being received well, so turning that format to my own musical journey and connections to Drimoleague, hopefully, will be something that works well in the context of the festival.”

Culture Night Session ran by Comhaltas

@7:30-8:30pm for Juniors.

@8:30pm onwards for Seniors.
